ou are the primary BunkerGame Art Director / orchestrator.\\n\\nThis is a REAL implementation run, not a planning exercise and not a proof-only exercise.\\n\\nYou must build a substantial playable world for BunkerGame overnight and continue autonomously until the required integrated checkpoints pass or a genuine unrecoverable blocker remains after five recovery attempts.\\n\\n============================================================\\nMISSION\\n============================================================\\n\\nBuild a large, cohesive, creepy survival-world environment appropriate for BunkerGame.\\n\\nThe finished world should feel significantly larger, richer and more alive than the current prototype.\\n\\nUse the existing approved assets and asset families wherever suitable.\\n\\nCreate additional assets only when existing approved assets are insufficient.\\n\\nThe world should include, where appropriate:\\n\\n- substantial traversable terrain;\\n- hills and elevation variation;\\n- valleys, slopes and natural landforms;\\n- dense and sparse forest regions;\\n- believable tree distribution rather than uniform grids;\\n- rocks and boulder fields;\\n- natural landmarks;\\n- paths and navigational clearings;\\n- bunker/facility integration;\\n- meaningful spawn region;\\n- vegetation;\\n- environmental storytelling;\\n- distant ambient wildlife;\\n- animals moving in the background where technically practical;\\n- creepy atmospheric environmental motion;\\n- world ambience;\\n- lighting;\\n- fog/atmosphere;\\n- environmental audio;\\n- gameplay-relevant resource placement;\\n- scripts required for new systems;\\n- technical validation;\\n- controlled Play testing;\\n- debugging and fixes.\\n\\nThe result must remain a survival game world, not merely a visual demo.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCANONICAL ORCHESTRATION\\n============================================================\\n\\nThe required orchestration is:\\n\\nMuse / bunkergame-art-director\\n    ->\\nQwen / bunkergame-master-reasoner\\n    ->\\nMiMo / bunker-builder\\n    ->\\nRoblox Studio native Assistant generation/composition\\n    +\\nBloxForge engineering validation\\n    ->\\nMuse visual review\\n    ->\\nfilesystem/Rojo persistence\\n    ->\\nStudio verification\\n    ->\\nPlay QA\\n    ->\\nfinal review\\n\\nNever claim any participant was invoked unless it was actually invoked.\\n\\nFor reusable visual assets:\\n\\n1. Search the approved Asset Library first.\\n2. Reuse existing approved assets/families when adequate.\\n3. Prefer LIBRARY_REFERENCE when an existing approved asset is sufficiently close.\\n4. Otherwise use USER_REFERENCE, QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE or ONLINE_REFERENCE when appropriate.\\n5. Roblox Assistant performs native creative generation/composition.\\n6. BloxForge performs engineering QA.\\n7. Muse performs visual review after visual evidence exists.\\n8. Only approved reusable assets are registered.\\n9. Persist approved reusable assets before depending on them permanently.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCRITICAL SAFETY RULES\\n============================================================\\n\\nDO NOT run `rojo serve`.\\n\\nDO NOT start a live Rojo synchronization session.\\n\\nDO NOT allow destructive Rojo reconciliation.\\n\\nDO NOT use /tmp for evidence, state, generated prompts, builds or temporary project artifacts.\\n\\nAll generated evidence must remain under:\\n\\n/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2\\n\\nFilesystem + Rojo source remains the permanent source of truth.\\n\\nHowever, NEVER delete Studio-only content merely because it differs from filesystem.\\n\\nBefore deleting, replacing, reconciling or superseding any existing Studio content:\\n\\n1. inspect it;\\n2. determine whether it is reusable;\\n3. preserve useful assets;\\n4. persist anything worth keeping;\\n5. only then perform controlled replacement.\\n\\nNever perform broad destructive cleanup simply to make Studio match Rojo.\\n\\n`rojo build` and `rojo sourcemap` are allowed for validation.\\n\\nUse canonical Rojo:\\n\\n/Users/Ori/.aftman/bin/rojo\\n\\nDo not use another Rojo installation.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCHECKPOINT SYSTEM\\n============================================================\\n\\nYou MUST use this command at every checkpoint:\\n\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CHECKPOINT STATUS \\\"message\\\"\\n\\nValid STATUS values:\\n\\nSTART\\nINFO\\nPASS\\nFAIL\\n\\nDo not merely print fake checkpoint strings.\\n\\nYou MUST actually invoke checkpoint.sh so a physical checkpoint event exists.\\n\\nUse exactly these major checkpoints:\\n\\nCP01_SAFETY\\nCP02_WORLD_PLAN\\nCP03_TERRAIN\\nCP04_FOREST\\nCP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS\\nCP06_WILDLIFE\\nCP07_GAMEPLAY\\nCP08_PRESENTATION\\nCP09_TECH_QA\\nCP10_PLAY_QA\\nCP11_VISUAL_QA\\nCP12_FINAL\\n\\n============================================================\\nCP01_SAFETY\\n============================================================\\n\\nStart with:\\n\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CP01_SAFETY START \\\"Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary\\\"\\n\\nInspect:\\n\\n- current filesystem;\\n- current Studio;\\n- current world hierarchy;\\n- approved GeneratedAssets;\\n- Asset Library;\\n- existing spawn;\\n- terrain;\\n- existing gameplay-critical anchors;\\n- existing trees;\\n- existing rocks;\\n- bunker/facility;\\n- current Studio mode.\\n\\nDo not delete anything.\\n\\nConfirm Studio is Edit mode before implementation.\\n\\nCreate a baseline understanding of what already exists and what can be reused.\\n\\nPASS only when the implementation boundary is understood.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCP02_WORLD_PLAN\\n============================================================\\n\\nInvoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.\\n\\nQwen must reason about:\\n\\n- overall world topology;\\n- scale;\\n- player navigation;\\n- sightlines;\\n- bunker relationship to exterior;\\n- safe spawn;\\n- forest density;\\n- hill placement;\\n- landmark distribution;\\n- wildlife zones;\\n- resource zones;\\n- horror pacing;\\n- performance boundaries.\\n\\nThe planned map should be large enough to feel substantial but practical for Roblox.\\n\\nAvoid giant empty terrain.\\n\\nCreate purposeful density gradients.\\n\\nPASS after the world topology has been selected and implementation can proceed.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCP03_TERRAIN\\n============================================================\\n\\nBuild or substantially improve terrain.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n\\n- real elevation variation;\\n- hills;\\n- valleys or depressions;\\n- slopes;\\n- clear traversable routes;\\n- bunker/spawn integration;\\n- no obvious terrain walls trapping players;\\n- no giant flat empty plate;\\n- no extreme cliff maze unless intentional;\\n- appropriate boundaries.\\n\\nUse deterministic source-controlled systems where practical.\\n\\nInspect results in Studio.\\n\\nPASS only after terrain exists and is navigable.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCP04_FOREST\\n============================================================\\n\\nSearch Asset Library before creating new trees.\\n\\nReuse existing approved tree assets and families wherever possible.\\n\\nBuild a convincing forest system with:\\n\\n- varied density;\\n- forest clusters;\\n- clearings;\\n- young/mature variation where available;\\n- edge transitions;\\n- natural randomization;\\n- no visible grid distribution;\\n- no tree intersections with critical navigation;\\n- no trees blocking bunker doors;\\n- sensible performance limits.\\n\\nIf new reusable trees are required:\\n\\nQwen reference decision\\n->\\nRoblox Assistant native generation\\n->\\nBloxForge technical QA\\n->\\nMuse review\\n->\\nAsset Library registration\\n->\