BRARY_REFERENCE when an existing approved asset is sufficiently close.\\n4. Otherwise use USER_REFERENCE, QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE or ONLINE_REFERENCE when appropriate.\\n5. Roblox Assistant performs native creative generation/composition.\\n6. BloxForge performs engineering QA.\\n7. Muse performs visual review after visual evidence exists.\\n8. Only approved reusable assets are registered.\\n9. Persist approved reusable assets before depending on them permanently.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCRITICAL SAFETY RULES\\n============================================================\\n\\nDO NOT run `rojo serve`.\\n\\nDO NOT start a live Rojo synchronization session.\\n\\nDO NOT allow destructive Rojo reconciliation.\\n\\nDO NOT use /tmp for evidence, state, generated prompts, builds or temporary project artifacts.\\n\\nAll generated evidence must remain under:\\n\\n/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2\\n\\nFilesystem + Rojo source remains the permanent source of truth.\\n\\nHowever, NEVER delete Studio-only content merely because it differs from filesystem.\\n\\nBefore deleting, replacing, reconciling or superseding any existing Studio content:\\n\\n1. inspect it;\\n2. determine whether it is reusable;\\n3. preserve useful assets;\\n4. persist anything worth keeping;\\n5. only then perform controlled replacement.\\n\\nNever perform broad destructive cleanup simply to make Studio match Rojo.\\n\\n`rojo build` and `rojo sourcemap` are allowed for validation.\\n\\nUse canonical Rojo:\\n\\n/Users/Ori/.aftman/bin/rojo\\n\\nDo not use another Rojo installation.\\n\\n============================================================\\nCHECKPOINT SYSTEM\\n============================================================\\n\\nYou MUST use this command at every checkpoint:\\n\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CHECKPOINT STATUS \\\"message\\\"\\n\\nValid STATUS values:\\n\\nSTART\\nINFO\\nPASS\\nFAIL\\n\\nDo not