{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788163213538,"sessionID":"ses_fa92d6ceeffefUV6TlT3Qq1n1K","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a056d5424072f186eedbb9cb5ff992","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2/events.log\necho \"---\"\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2/state.txt\necho \"---\"\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md 2>&1 | head -n 80\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/TECH-BIBLE.md 2>&1 | head -n 80\n"},"output":"2026-08-31 10:36:10|CP01_SAFETY|START|Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary\n2026-08-31 10:36:48|CP01_SAFETY|PASS|Studio Edit verified, filesystem GameWorld intact, Studio divergence noted — GameWorld currently in ServerStorage.NOT IN USE, Workspace empty but source preserved, safety boundary established\n2026-08-31 10:36:50|CP02_WORLD_PLAN|START|Invoking Qwen master-reasoner for large creepy survival world topology\n---\nRUN_ATTEMPT_2\n---\n# THE OUTSKIRTS — Game Vision\n\n## Identity\n\n**Game:** THE OUTSKIRTS\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS is an atmospheric survival game. The target is a polished,\ncohesive experience rather than a basic Roblox blockout or a collection of\nunconnected systems.\n\n## Target Experience\n\nThe player should feel vulnerable, curious, and motivated to make an abandoned\nplace functional again. Environments, gameplay systems, lighting, sound, UI,\nand progression should ultimately support the same survival atmosphere.\n\nThe intended quality bar is:\n\n- atmospheric\n- detailed\n- intentionally composed\n- abandoned but functional\n- survival-oriented\n- visually cohesive\n- significantly more polished than the current bunker\n\n## Starting Experience\n\nThe player wakes near an old bed inside a creepy, abandoned underground bunker\nbedroom.\n\nThe bedroom is the first readable space in a larger bunker. It must establish:\n\n- where the player has awakened\n- that the bunker is old, neglected, and still partly functional\n- a clear visual route toward the rest of the bunker\n- the survival tone of the wider game\n\nThe bedroom must connect into a larger bunker. It is not an isolated box and\nmust not be treated as a standalone final environment.\n\n## Bunker Vision\n\nThe bunker should be a sequence of purposeful, connected spaces rather than one\nrectangular room. The layout should eventually support:\n\n- bedroom/start area\n- central bunker/common area\n- weapon/workbench area\n- upgrade area\n- storage\n- power/electrical infrastructure\n- NPC/shop area\n- access toward farming and the outside\n- bunker entrance/defense point\n\nThese are spatial and long-term functional requirements. Missing gameplay\nbehavior must not be invented during environment planning.\n\n## Broader Gameplay Vision\n\nLong-term concepts include:\n\n- realistic-feeling rifle and combat gameplay\n- pickaxe/tool gameplay\n- torch/flashlight gameplay\n- farming with multiple crops, including wheat and carrots\n- improved zombies\n- wave survival\n- NPC shop\n- progression\n- polished UI\n- multiple maps and biomes\n\nThese items describe direction only. They are not permission to implement a\nsystem unless a specific approved task defines it.\n\n## Quality and Scope Rules\n\n- Do not treat the rejected bedroom blockout as approved composition or art.\n# BunkerGame — Technical Bible\n\n## Authority\n\nServer owns trusted gameplay state.\n\nClient owns:\n- presentation\n- input\n- UI\n- camera effects\n- non-authoritative visual feedback\n\n## Source of Truth\n\nFilesystem + Rojo project.\n\n## Rojo Mapping\n\nAlways read `default.project.json` before making assumptions about filesystem-to-Roblox mappings.\n\nDo not invent mappings.\n\n## BDS 4\n\nAvailable commands:\n- bds doctor\n- bds inspect\n- bds ast <file>\n- bds review project\n- bds review all\n\nDo not use:\n- bds analyze\n- bds file\n- bds range\n\nThese commands do not exist in the current BDS 4 installation.\n\n## Workflow\n\nBefore implementation:\n\ntools/workflows/preflight.sh\n\nAfter implementation:\n- run bds ast on every changed Luau file\n- run tools/workflows/postflight.sh\n\n## Evidence Policy\n\nNever invent:\n- files\n- RemoteEvents\n- APIs\n- ModuleScripts\n- assets\n- Rojo mappings\n\nUninspected RBXM content must be labeled:\n\nUNVERIFIED_BINARY\n\n## Implementation Rule\n\nWhen a technical specification exists in docs/director, execute it rather than redesigning it.\n\nIf the specification conflicts with verified project evidence:\n- stop\n- show the evidence\n- report the conflict\n- do not improvise\n","metadata":{"output":"2026-08-31 10:36:10|CP01_SAFETY|START|Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary\n2026-08-31 10:36:48|CP01_SAFETY|PASS|Studio Edit verified, filesystem GameWorld intact, Studio divergence noted — GameWorld currently in ServerStorage.NOT IN USE, Workspace empty but source preserved, safety boundary established\n2026-08-31 10:36:50|CP02_WORLD_PLAN|START|Invoking Qwen master-reasoner for large creepy survival world topology\n---\nRUN_ATTEMPT_2\n---\n# THE OUTSKIRTS — Game Vision\n\n## Identity\n\n**Game:** THE OUTSKIRTS\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS is an atmospheric survival game. The target is a polished,\ncohesive experience rather than a basic Roblox blockout or a collection of\nunconnected systems.\n\n## Target Experience\n\nThe player should feel vulnerable, curious, and motivated to make an abandoned\nplace functional again. Environments, gameplay systems, lighting, sound, UI,\nand progression should ultimately support the same survival atmosphere.\n\nThe intended quality bar is:\n\n- atmospheric\n- detailed\n- intentionally composed\n- abandoned but functional\n- survival-oriented\n- visually cohesive\n- significantly more polished than the current bunker\n\n## Starting Experience\n\nThe player wakes near an old bed inside a creepy, abandoned underground bunker\nbedroom.\n\nThe bedroom is the first readable space in a larger bunker. It must establish:\n\n- where the player has awakened\n- that the bunker is old, neglected, and still partly functional\n- a clear visual route toward the rest of the bunker\n- the survival tone of the wider game\n\nThe bedroom must connect into a larger bunker. It is not an isolated box and\nmust not be treated as a standalone final environment.\n\n## Bunker Vision\n\nThe bunker should be a sequence of purposeful, connected spaces rather than one\nrectangular room. The layout should eventually support:\n\n- bedroom/start area\n- central bunker/common area\n- weapon/workbench area\n- upgrade area\n- storage\n- power/electrical infrastructure\n- NPC/shop area\n- access toward farming and the outside\n- bunker entrance/defense point\n\nThese are spatial and long-term functional requirements. Missing gameplay\nbehavior must not be invented during environment planning.\n\n## Broader Gameplay Vision\n\nLong-term concepts include:\n\n- realistic-feeling rifle and combat gameplay\n- pickaxe/tool gameplay\n- torch/flashlight gameplay\n- farming with multiple crops, including wheat and carrots\n- improved zombies\n- wave survival\n- NPC shop\n- progression\n- polished UI\n- multiple maps and biomes\n\nThese items describe direction only. They are not permission to implement a\nsystem unless a specific approved task defines it.\n\n## Quality and Scope Rules\n\n- Do not treat the rejected bedroom blockout as approved composition or art.\n# BunkerGame — Technical Bible\n\n## Authority\n\nServer owns trusted gameplay state.\n\nClient owns:\n- presentation\n- input\n- UI\n- camera effects\n- non-authoritative visual feedback\n\n## Source of Truth\n\nFilesystem + Rojo project.\n\n## Rojo Mapping\n\nAlways read `default.project.json` before making assumptions about filesystem-to-Roblox mappings.\n\nDo not invent mappings.\n\n## BDS 4\n\nAvailable commands:\n- bds doctor\n- bds inspect\n- bds ast <file>\n- bds review project\n- bds review all\n\nDo not use:\n- bds analyze\n- bds file\n- bds range\n\nThese commands do not exist in the current BDS 4 installation.\n\n## Workflow\n\nBefore implementation:\n\ntools/workflows/preflight.sh\n\nAfter implementation:\n- run bds ast on every changed Luau file\n- run tools/workflows/postflight.sh\n\n## Evidence Policy\n\nNever invent:\n- files\n- RemoteEvents\n- APIs\n- ModuleScripts\n- assets\n- Rojo mappings\n\nUninspected RBXM content must be labeled:\n\nUNVERIFIED_BINARY\n\n## Implementation Rule\n\nWhen a technical specification exists in docs/director, execute it rather than redesigning it.\n\nIf the specification conflicts with verified project evidence:\n- stop\n- show the evidence\n- report the conflict\n- do not improvise\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2/events.log\necho \"---\"\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2/state.txt\necho \"---\"\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md 2>&1 | head -n 80\ncat /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/TECH-BIBLE.md 2>&1 | head -n 80\n","time":{"start":1788163213525,"end":1788163213529}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a056d5424072f186eedbb9cb5ff992"}},"id":"prt_056d54268001KxvsBCERC1bBNE","sessionID":"ses_fa92d6ceeffefUV6TlT3Qq1n1K","messageID":"msg_056d53ce0001WD1939hWwD2rel"}}
