========\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBuild a large, cohesive, creepy survival-world environment appropriate for BunkerGame.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe finished world should feel significantly larger, richer and more alive than the current prototype.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUse the existing approved assets and asset families wherever suitable.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCreate additional assets only when existing approved assets are insufficient.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe world should include, where appropriate:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- substantial traversable terrain;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- hills and elevation variation;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- valleys, slopes and natural landforms;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- dense and sparse forest regions;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- believable tree distribution rather than uniform grids;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- rocks and boulder fields;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- natural landmarks;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- paths and navigational clearings;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- bunker/facility integration;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- meaningful spawn region;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- vegetation;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- environmental storytelling;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- distant ambient wildlife;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- animals moving in the background where technically practical;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- creepy atmospheric environmental motion;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- world ambience;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- lightin\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"...\\n\\nA\\\\\\\\nCP12_FINAL\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP01_SAFETY\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStart with:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CP01_SAFETY START \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInspect:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- current filesystem;\\\\\\\\n- current Studio;\\\\\\\\n- current world hierarchy;\\\\\\\\n- approved GeneratedAssets;\\\\\\\\n- Asset Library;\\\\\\\\n- existing spawn;\\\\\\\\n- terrain;\\\\\\\\n- existing gameplay-critical anchors;\\\\\\\\n- existing trees;\\\\\\\\n- existing rocks;\\\\\\\\n- bunker/facility;\\\\\\\\n- current Studio mode.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDo not delete anything.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nConfirm Studio is Edit mode before implementation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCreate a baseline understanding of what already exists and what can be reused.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS only when the implementation boundary is understood.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP02_WORLD_PLAN\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInvoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nQwen must reason about:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- overall world topology;\\\\\\\\n- scale;\\\\\\\\n- player navigation;\\\\\\\\n- sightlines;\\\\\\\\n- bunker relationship to exterior;\\\\\\\\n- safe spawn;\\\\\\\\n- forest density;\\\\\\\\n- hill placement;\\\\\\\\n- landmark distribution;\\\\\\\\n- wildlife zones;\\\\\\\\n- resource zones;\\\\\\\\n- horror pacing;\\\\\\\\n- performance boundaries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe planned map should be large enough to feel substantial but practical for Roblox.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAvoid giant empty terrain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCreate purposeful density gradients.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS after the world topology has been selected and implementation can proceed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP03_TERRAIN\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBuild or substantially improve terrain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- real elevation variation;\\\\\\\\n- hills;\\\\\\\\n- valleys or depressions;\\\\\\\\n- slopes;\\\\\\\\n- clear traversable routes;\\\\\\\\n- bunker/spawn integration;\\\\\\\\n- no obvious terrain walls trapping players;\\\\\\\\n- no giant flat empty plate;\\\\\\\\n- no extreme cliff maze unless intentional;\\\\\\\\n- appropriate boundaries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse deterministic source-controlled systems where practical.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInspect results in Studio.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS only after terrain exists and is navigable.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP04_FOREST\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSearch Asset Library before creating new trees.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReuse existing approved tree assets and families wherever possible.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBuild a convincing forest system with:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- varied density;\\\\\\\\n- forest clusters;\\\\\\\\n- clearings;\\\\\\\\n- young/mature variation where available;\\\\\\\\n- edge transitions;\\\\\\\\n- natural randomization;\\\\\\\\n- no visible grid distribution;\\\\\\\\n- no tree intersections with critical navigation;\\\\\\\\n- no trees blocking bunker doors;\\\\\\\\n- sensible performance limits.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIf new reusable trees are required:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nQwen reference decision\\\\\\\\n->\\\\\\\\nRoblox Assistant native generation\\\\\\\\n->\\\\\\\\nBloxForge technical QA\\\\\\\\n->\\\\\\\\nMuse review\\\\\\\\n->\\\\\\\\nAsset Library registration\\\\\\\\n->\\\\\\\\nfilesystem persistence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS only after the world has substantial forest coverage and navigation remains usable.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReuse approved boulder and rock assets first.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAdd:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- individual boulders;\\\\\\\\n- rock clusters;\\\\\\\\n- terrain-supported formations;\\\\\\\\n- landmarks;\\\\\\\\n- visual navigation anchors;\\\\\\\\n- composition around paths and bunker approaches.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAvoid random prop spam.\\\\\\\\n---LAST LOGS---\\\\\\\\n[2026-08-31 10:27:40] STATE=PREFLIGHT\\\\\\\\n[2026-