=======================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInvoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nQwen must reason about:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- overall world topology;\\\\\\\\n- scale;\\\\\\\\n- player navigation;\\\\\\\\n- sightlines;\\\\\\\\n- bunker relationship to exterior;\\\\\\\\n- safe spawn;\\\\\\\\n- forest density;\\\\\\\\n- hill placement;\\\\\\\\n- landmark distribution;\\\\\\\\n- wildlife zones;\\\\\\\\n- resource zones;\\\\\\\\n- horror pacing;\\\\\\\\n- performance boundaries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe planned map should be large enough to feel substantial but practical for Roblox.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAvoid giant empty terrain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCreate purposeful density gradients.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS after the world topology has been selected and implementation can proceed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP03_TERRAIN\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBuild or substantially improve terrain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- real elevation variation;\\\\\\\\n- hills;\\\\\\\\n- valleys or depressions;\\\\\\\\n- slopes;\\\\\\\\n- clear traversable routes;\\\\\\\\n- bunker/spawn integration;\\\\\\\\n- no obvious terrain walls trapping players;\\\\\\\\n- no giant flat empty plate;\\\\\\\\n- no extreme cliff maze unless intentional;\\\\\\\\n- appropriate boundaries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse deterministic source-controlled systems where practical.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInspect results in Studio.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPASS only after terrain exists and is navigable.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\nCP04_FOREST\\\\\\\\n============================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSearch Asset Library before creating new trees.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReuse existing approved tree assets and families wherever possible.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBuild a convincing forest system with:\