mand at every checkpoint:\\\\n\\\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CHECKPOINT STATUS \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nValid STATUS values:\\\\n\\\\nSTART\\\\nINFO\\\\nPASS\\\\nFAIL\\\\n\\\\nDo not merely print fake checkpoint strings.\\\\n\\\\nYou MUST actually invoke checkpoint.sh so a physical checkpoint event exists.\\\\n\\\\nUse exactly these major checkpoints:\\\\n\\\\nCP01_SAFETY\\\\nCP02_WORLD_PLAN\\\\nCP03_TERRAIN\\\\nCP04_FOREST\\\\nCP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS\\\\nCP06_WILDLIFE\\\\nCP07_GAMEPLAY\\\\nCP08_PRESENTATION\\\\nCP09_TECH_QA\\\\nCP10_PLAY_QA\\\\nCP11_VISUAL_QA\\\\nCP12_FINAL\\\\n\\\\n============================================================\\\\nCP01_SAFETY\\\\n============================================================\\\\n\\\\nStart with:\\\\n\\\\n.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CP01_SAFETY START \\\\\\\"Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nInspect:\\\\n\\\\n- current filesystem;\\\\n- current Studio;\\\\n- current world hierarchy;\\\\n- approved GeneratedAssets;\\\\n- Asset Library;\\\\n- existing spawn;\\\\n- terrain;\\\\n- existing gameplay-critical anchors;\\\\n- existing trees;\\\\n- existing rocks;\\\\n- bunker/facility;\\\\n- current Studio mode.\\\\n\\\\nDo not delete anything.\\\\n\\\\nConfirm Studio is Edit mode before implementation.\\\\n\\\\nCreate a baseline understanding of what already exists and what can be reused.\\\\n\\\\nPASS only when the implementation boundary is understood.\\\\n\\\\n============================================================\\\\nCP02_WORLD_PLAN\\\\n============================================================\\\\n\\\\nInvoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.\\\\n\\\\nQwen must reason about:\\\\n\\\\n- overall world topology;\\\\n- scale;\\\\n- player navigation;\\\\n- sightlines;\\\\n- bunker relationship to exterior;\\\\n- safe spawn;\\\\n- forest density;\\\\n- hill placement;\\\\n- landmark distribution;\\\\n- wildlife zones;\\\\n- resource zones;\\\\n-