{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788164815315,"sessionID":"ses_fa9129debffeL21HVlIw3GkiIp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a056edb0677e519049ee612d63526f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat .opencode/overnight_world_v2/directive.txt 2>&1 | head -n 100\necho \"---\"\ncat docs/director/CURRENT-TASK.md 2>&1 | head -n 200\necho \"---\"\ncat default.project.json 2>&1\necho \"---\"\nls -R src 2>&1 | head -n 300\necho \"---\"\ncat .opencode/overnight_world_v2/state.txt\ncat .opencode/overnight_world_v2/last_run_exit.txt 2>&1 | head -n 100\n"},"output":"BUNKERGAME OVERNIGHT WORLD BUILD V2\n\nYou are the primary BunkerGame Art Director / orchestrator.\n\nThis is a REAL implementation run, not a planning exercise and not a proof-only exercise.\n\nYou must build a substantial playable world for BunkerGame overnight and continue autonomously until the required integrated checkpoints pass or a genuine unrecoverable blocker remains after five recovery attempts.\n\n============================================================\nMISSION\n============================================================\n\nBuild a large, cohesive, creepy survival-world environment appropriate for BunkerGame.\n\nThe finished world should feel significantly larger, richer and more alive than the current prototype.\n\nUse the existing approved assets and asset families wherever suitable.\n\nCreate additional assets only when existing approved assets are insufficient.\n\nThe world should include, where appropriate:\n\n- substantial traversable terrain;\n- hills and elevation variation;\n- valleys, slopes and natural landforms;\n- dense and sparse forest regions;\n- believable tree distribution rather than uniform grids;\n- rocks and boulder fields;\n- natural landmarks;\n- paths and navigational clearings;\n- bunker/facility integration;\n- meaningful spawn region;\n- vegetation;\n- environmental storytelling;\n- distant ambient wildlife;\n- animals moving in the background where technically practical;\n- creepy atmospheric environmental motion;\n- world ambience;\n- lighting;\n- fog/atmosphere;\n- environmental audio;\n- gameplay-relevant resource placement;\n- scripts required for new systems;\n- technical validation;\n- controlled Play testing;\n- debugging and fixes.\n\nThe result must remain a survival game world, not merely a visual demo.\n\n============================================================\nCANONICAL ORCHESTRATION\n============================================================\n\nThe required orchestration is:\n\nMuse / bunkergame-art-director\n    ->\nQwen / bunkergame-master-reasoner\n    ->\nMiMo / bunker-builder\n    ->\nRoblox Studio native Assistant generation/composition\n    +\nBloxForge engineering validation\n    ->\nMuse visual review\n    ->\nfilesystem/Rojo persistence\n    ->\nStudio verification\n    ->\nPlay QA\n    ->\nfinal review\n\nNever claim any participant was invoked unless it was actually invoked.\n\nFor reusable visual assets:\n\n1. Search the approved Asset Library first.\n2. Reuse existing approved assets/families when adequate.\n3. Prefer LIBRARY_REFERENCE when an existing approved asset is sufficiently close.\n4. Otherwise use USER_REFERENCE, QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE or ONLINE_REFERENCE when appropriate.\n5. Roblox Assistant performs native creative generation/composition.\n6. BloxForge performs engineering QA.\n7. Muse performs visual review after visual evidence exists.\n8. Only approved reusable assets are registered.\n9. Persist approved reusable assets before depending on them permanently.\n\n============================================================\nCRITICAL SAFETY RULES\n============================================================\n\nDO NOT run `rojo serve`.\n\nDO NOT start a live Rojo synchronization session.\n\nDO NOT allow destructive Rojo reconciliation.\n\nDO NOT use /tmp for evidence, state, generated prompts, builds or temporary project artifacts.\n---\n# CURRENT TASK\n\