{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788165928963,"sessionID":"ses_fa90d7edcffe1ucmkd4gJeyy9S","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a056f4e38c7aa0850f0353ebf4e154","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Build wildlife ambient system","prompt":"You are the BunkerGame bunker-builder implementer. Build CP06_WILDLIFE: restrained ambient wildlife.\n\nCONTEXT: Filesystem is source of truth at /Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame. Workspace.GameWorld is 640x640 with Foundation, Bunker, Exterior, Farm, Resources etc. Already passed CP03 terrain, CP04 forest (18 trees + 62 dressing), CP05 landmarks. Next must add wildlife.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n- Create server-authoritative, low-cost ambient wildlife.\n- Prefer pooled/reused agents, no per-frame heavy AI, server tick ~2-5 sec, not every heartbeat.\n- Scope: 3-5 distant deer-like silhouettes in forest perimeters + optional birds/small ambient via simple parts.\n- Must not block bunker doors or critical navigation, must be distant background.\n- Must not fall through terrain, must not spam part count beyond Performance.GameWorldMaximumBaseParts 2500.\n- Wildlife zones: west forest around X -140 to -195, Z 0-140 and east forest X 160-220, Z -30 to 70 ; keep Y approx 54 ground.\n- Movement: simple wander between 3-4 deterministic waypoint anchors, slow walk speed 4-6, anchored parts with CanCollide false.\n- Implement actual scripts: create new Service at src/ServerScriptService/Game/Services/WildlifeService.luau\n  - Start() spawns wildlife models under Workspace.Runtime.Wildlife (or Workspace.GameWorld.Exterior.WildlifeAnchors if you need anchors)\n  - Uses TweenService or CFrame lerping every ~3 sec, checks path not blocked.\n  - Expose GetWildlife() maybe? Keep simple.\n  - Register with ServiceBag via ServerBootstrap if needed (inspect ServerBootstrap to see pattern).\n- Add GameWorld model anchors: create Model \"Wildlife\" inside GameWorld.Exterior or as sibling. Include 4-5 spawn anchor Parts (anchored, invisible transparency 1, CanCollide false) at the forest perimeters with Position matching zones above. Anchors should have attributes WildlifeAnchor=true.\n- Create deer model template: simple blocky deer using Primitive parts (Body Part, Head Part, 4 Leg Parts) grouped as Model with PrimaryPart Body, all Anchored, CanCollide false, CastShadow true. Size small (~2x1.5x3 body, head 1x1x1, legs 0.3x1x1). Color earth tones. This must be cloned at runtime, not baked as 50 deer. Only anchors in GameWorld, deer models instantiated in Runtime folder.\n- For birds: add 2-3 invisible AudioAnchors or VFXAnchors that periodically play a bird sound or show a small moving part overhead at high Y (70-80) traversing linearly — optional if feasible without extra sounds. If sound not available, just use moving part silhouette (small 0.5 part moving across sky every 45 sec).\n- Ensure scripts handle cleanup on Stop(), disconnect connections, destroy runtime clones.\n- Validate: Run BDS AST or luau check via /Users/Ori/.aftman/bin/rojo sourcemap and ensure no syntax errors. Ensure wildlife does not intersect bunker, paths remain clear, performance budget ok.\n- Evidence: ensure file persists under src/..., Rojo build succeeds, and make a small validation log under .opencode/overnight_world_v2/evidence/wildlife_validation.txt\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Do NOT run rojo serve.\n- Do NOT delete Studio-only content.\n- Keep existing GameWorld structure intact — only add new Wildlife nodes.\n- Deterministic positions, RuntimeRandomness false compliance — use fixed waypoint positions, not math.random without seed? Use fixed offsets.\n- Horror pacing: wildlife should be distant, occasional, not cartoonish herd in center.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n- src/ServerScriptService/Game/Services/WildlifeService.luau\n- Modified src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json adding Wildlife anchors (and optionally a template folder)\n- Modified src/ReplicatedStorage/Game/WorldManifest.luau if needed? No, wildlife anchors not validated by WorldService, so keep separate to avoid breaking validation (do not add to Manifest).\n- Ensure ServerBootstrap loads WildlifeService (check its list).\n\nAfter implementation, report:\n- Files changed\n- Part counts added\n- How movement works and its tick rate\n- How you verified no collisions with Bunker/paths\n- Rojo sourcemap/build result\n\nKeep changes minimal and reversible. Use deterministic source-controlled logic.","subagent_type":"bunker-builder"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_fa90ae36effeI46vIuS7unMAkw\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nThe sourcemap confirms WildlifeService is properly mapped. The model JSON children (like Wildlife anchors) are resolved at Rojo sync time, not in the sourcemap — this is expected Rojo behavior.\n\n---\n\n## CP06 WILDLIFE — HANDOFF REPORT\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Status | Description |\n|------|--------|-------------|\n| `src/ServerScriptService/Game/Services/WildlifeService.luau` | **NEW** | Server-authoritative ambient wildlife service (377 lines) |\n| `src/ServerScriptService/Game/ServerBootstrap.server.luau` | **MODIFIED** | Added WildlifeService import + ServiceBag registration |\n| `src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json` | **MODIFIED** | Added `GameWorld.Exterior.Wildlife` model with 8 anchor parts |\n\n### Part Counts Added\n\n- **8 permanent source-of-truth anchor parts** in `GameWorld.Exterior.Wildlife` (all invisible, CanCollide false)\n- **33 runtime parts** created at service Start (5 deer × 6 parts + 3 bird parts), destroyed at Stop\n- **Combined: 41 parts** — well within `GameWorldMaximumBaseParts` budget of 2500\n\n### Movement Architecture\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Tick rate** | 3-second interval via `task.delay` loop (not Heartbeat) |\n| **Deer speed** | 5 studs/sec via TweenService CFrame tween |\n| **Bird speed** | 18 studs/sec, 45-sec period between crossings |\n| **Waypoints** | 10 hardcoded positions, 5 deer cycle deterministically |\n| **No per-frame AI** | TweenService handles interpolation; server only advances waypoints every 3 sec |\n\n### Collision / Navigation Safety\n\n- **West forest deer**: X -148 to -185, Z 25-110 — closest to bunker wall at X=-62 is 86 studs away\n- **East forest deer**: X 175-210, Z -15 to 60 — closest to bunker wall at X=+58 is 117 studs away\n- **Birds**: Y=75 altitude, far overhead, no collision\n- **All wildlife CanCollide=false** — zero navigation blocking\n\n### Deterministic Compliance\n\n- All waypoint positions: hardcoded constants (no `math.random`)\n- `RuntimeRandomness: false` on GameWorld — compliant\n- Deer start indices: fixed array `{ 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 }`\n\n### Validation Results\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| `bds ast WildlifeService.luau` | **HAS_ERROR=False** |\n| `bds ast ServerBootstrap.server.luau` | **HAS_ERROR=False** |\n| `rojo sourcemap` | **SUCCESS** — WildlifeService mapped |\n| JSON validity | **PASS** — Wildlife correctly nested in Exterior |\n| Evidence file | `.opencode/overnight_world_v2/evidence/wildlife_validation.txt` |\n\n### Horizon Pacing\n\nWildlife is distant, sparse, and restrained — 5 deer silhouettes in forest perimeters, 3 birds crossing overhead. They never approach the bunker center. The 3-second tick rate with slow tween movement creates a subtle, atmospheric background presence appropriate for horror pacing.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_fa90d7edcffe1ucmkd4gJeyy9S","sessionId":"ses_fa90ae36effeI46vIuS7unMAkw","model":{"providerID":"opencode","modelID":"mimo-v2.5-free"},"truncated":false},"title":"Build wildlife ambient system","time":{"start":1788165299367,"end":1788165928915}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a056f4e38c7aa0850f0353ebf4e154"}},"id":"prt_056f4e36b001y74AEncGBlBXG0","sessionID":"ses_fa90d7edcffe1ucmkd4gJeyy9S","messageID":"msg_056f4d6f000111qmN2R6u1z6jE"}}
