ing;\\012- debugging and fixes.\\012\\012The result must remain a survival game world, not merely a visual demo.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CANONICAL ORCHESTRATION\\012============================================================\\012\\012The required orchestration is:\\012\\012Muse / bunkergame-art-director\\012    ->\\012Qwen / bunkergame-master-reasoner\\012    ->\\012MiMo / bunker-builder\\012    ->\\012Roblox Studio native Assistant generation/composition\\012    +\\012BloxForge engineering validation\\012    ->\\012Muse visual review\\012    ->\\012filesystem/Rojo persistence\\012    ->\\012Studio verification\\012    ->\\012Play QA\\012    ->\\012final review\\012\\012Never claim any participant was invoked unless it was actually invoked.\\012\\012For reusable visual assets:\\012\\0121. Search the approved Asset Library first.\\0122. Reuse existing approved assets/families when adequate.\\0123. Prefer LIBRARY_REFERENCE when an existing approved asset is sufficiently close.\\0124. Otherwise use USER_REFERENCE, QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE or ONLINE_REFERENCE when appropriate.\\0125. Roblox Assistant performs native creative generation/composition.\\0126. BloxForge performs engineering QA.\\0127. Muse performs visual review after visual evidence exists.\\0128. Only approved reusable assets are registered.\\0129. Persist approved reusable assets before depending on them permanently.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CRITICAL SAFETY RULES\\012============================================================\\012\\012DO NOT run `rojo serve`.\\012\\012DO NOT start a live Rojo synchronization session.\\012\\012DO NOT allow destructive Rojo reconciliation.\\012\\012DO NOT use /tmp for evidence, state, generated prompts, builds or temporary project artifacts.\\012\\012All generated evidence must remain under:\\012\\012/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2\\012\