lay-critical anchors;\\012- existing trees;\\012- existing rocks;\\012- bunker/facility;\\012- current Studio mode.\\012\\012Do not delete anything.\\012\\012Confirm Studio is Edit mode before implementation.\\012\\012Create a baseline understanding of what already exists and what can be reused.\\012\\012PASS only when the implementation boundary is understood.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CP02_WORLD_PLAN\\012============================================================\\012\\012Invoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.\\012\\012Qwen must reason about:\\012\\012- overall world topology;\\012- scale;\\012- player navigation;\\012- sightlines;\\012- bunker relationship to exterior;\\012- safe spawn;\\012- forest density;\\012- hill placement;\\012- landmark distribution;\\012- wildlife zones;\\012- resource zones;\\012- horror pacing;\\012- performance boundaries.\\012\\012The planned map should be large enough to feel substantial but practical for Roblox.\\012\\012Avoid giant empty terrain.\\012\\012Create purposeful density gradients.\\012\\012PASS after the world topology has been selected and implementation can proceed.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CP03_TERRAIN\\012============================================================\\012\\012Build or substantially improve terrain.\\012\\012Requirements:\\012\\012- real elevation variation;\\012- hills;\\012- valleys or depressions;\\012- slopes;\\012- clear traversable routes;\\012- bunker/spawn integration;\\012- no obvious terrain walls trapping players;\\012- no giant flat empty plate;\\012- no extreme cliff maze unless intentional;\\012- appropriate boundaries.\\012\\012Use deterministic source-controlled systems where practical.\\012\\012Inspect results in Studio.\\012\\012PASS only after terrain exists and is navigable.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CP04_FOREST\\012============================================================\\012\\012Search Asset Library before creating new trees.\\012\\012Reuse existing approved tree assets and families wherever possible.\\012\\012Build a convincing forest system with:\\012\\012- varied density;\\012- forest clusters;\\012- clearings;\\012- young/mature variation where available;\\012- edge transitions;\\012- natural randomization;\\012- no visible grid distribution;\\012- no tree intersections with critical navigation;\\012- no trees blocking bunker doors;\\012- sensible performance limits.\\012\\012If new reusable trees are required:\\012\\012Qwen reference decision\\012->\\012Roblox Assistant native generation\\012->\\012BloxForge technical QA\\012->\\012Muse review\\012->\\012Asset Library registration\\012->\\012filesystem persistence.\\012\\012PASS only after the world has substantial forest coverage and navigation remains usable.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS\\012============================================================\\012\\012Reuse approved boulder and rock assets first.\\012\\012Add:\\012\\012- individual boulders;\\012- rock clusters;\\012- terrain-supported formations;\\012- landmarks;\\012- visual navigation anchors;\\012- composition around paths and bunker approaches.\\012\\012Avoid random prop spam.\\012\\012Avoid floating/intersecting rocks.\\012\\012BloxForge must validate scale, collision, anchoring, orientation and placement for reusable assets.\\012\\012PASS after landmarks materially improve world readability.\\012\\012============================================================\\012CP06_WILDLIFE\\012============================================================\\012\\012Add restrained ambient wildlife if technically feasible.\\012\\012Examples may include:\\012\\012- deer-like distant animals;\\012- birds;\\012- small ambient creatures;\\012- silhouettes moving through distant forest.\\012\\012Wildlife should support atmosphere